<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en" class="[scrollbar-gutter:stable]">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <meta name="csrf-token" content={get_csrf_token()} />
    <.live_title suffix=" · Phoenix Framework">
      {assigns[:page_title] || "Fullstack"}
    </.live_title>
    <%!--
      Resolve the theme before first paint. Setting it from LiveView instead
      would flash the wrong theme on every load while the socket connects.
      localStorage throws outright in some privacy modes, hence the try/catch.
    --%>
    <script>
      try {
        var saved = localStorage.getItem("theme");
        var sys = window.matchMedia("(prefers-color-scheme: dark)").matches;
        document.documentElement.dataset.theme = saved || (sys ? "dark" : "light");
      } catch (_) {
        document.documentElement.dataset.theme = "light";
      }
    </script>
    <link phx-track-static rel="stylesheet" href={~p"/assets/app.css"} />
    <script defer phx-track-static type="text/javascript" src={~p"/assets/app.js"}>
    </script>
    <%!--
      Fallback font load for the /waitlist page's scoped design (see
      odd/tasks/waitlist-landing-page.md, Round 3). Phoenix LiveView 1.2 has
      no per-LiveView <head> injection mechanism, and /waitlist shares this
      app's single root layout / :browser pipeline with every other route,
      so there is no clean way to load this stylesheet only on that page.
      This is just a font stylesheet load (no new CSS rules), scoped CSS for
      the design itself lives entirely in that LiveView's own template under
      the .wl class.
    --%>
    <link
      rel="stylesheet"
      href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Fraunces:opsz,wght@9..144,400;9..144,500;9..144,600;9..144,700&family=Inter:wght@400;500;600;700&family=JetBrains+Mono:wght@400;500;600&display=swap"
    />
  </head>
  <body class="bg-base-100 text-base-content antialiased">
    <a
      href="#main-content"
      class="sr-only focus:not-sr-only focus:absolute focus:z-50 focus:top-2 focus:left-2 focus:rounded-lg focus:bg-primary focus:px-4 focus:py-2 focus:text-primary-content focus:font-semibold focus-visible:outline focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-base-content"
    >
      Skip to main content
    </a>
    {@inner_content}
  </body>
</html>
